forgeVideo({"file": "01-brief-elicitation.en.html-player.js", "lang": "en", "title": "How a brief is born", "section": "Tutorial", "name": "How a brief is born: questions, research, the write, the lock", "date": "28. 9. 2026", "pace": [4.0, 8.0, 16.0], "duration": 1009.0, "events": [{"k": "card", "title": "How a brief is born", "text": ["Real work, not a demo. Three sessions of one day, 28 September 2026: from the first word at 08:46 to the lock at 18:36 about ten hours passed.", "This is a cut. The times are real, the lines of the terminal verbatim, only shortened. The hours of work over wording, the saves to git and the second review between the scenes are not here."], "dur": 10.0}, {"k": "card", "title": "What you will see", "text": ["A brief is found by questions and proposals: Claude proposes, the principal decides.", "Nothing is written without the principal's word; what lives only in the conversation is \"nowhere yet\".", "One item per message, a verdict of one letter, one write at the end of the round.", "A critique from outside and a research are steps the principal orders and judges.", "The lock is his explicit act: from then on the brief is immutable and is mined into the intent."], "dur": 11.875}, {"k": "scene", "no": 1, "time": "08:46", "title": "The spark", "caption": [["Now", "The principal throws a proposal into the conversation: align the elicitations and cut into the split of the engine. Claude takes it apart, says his opinion and asks one question. Three exchanges later it turns out the topic is a whole of thinking, and the brief is born on the principal's word."], ["Why", "A brief is not born from an outline but from a rough thought. Claude proposes the steps, the principal chooses them, and a new document comes into being only on his word."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "my proposal. lets tune the elicitations so they share a common mechanism (shouldnt the recipe elicitation be /forge recipe?) and shape and IMO we will have to cut into that engine split", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I read the proposal this way, three pieces:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. One mechanism of elicitation for everything composed with the principal: a definition + a skeleton, one pair per kind of document. Today it exists twice – /forge states and /recipe genres.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. /forge recipe <genre> [name] in place of /recipe. My opinion: yes, it fits. A recipe is a versioned document with an elicitation, the same kind of thing as a brief or a BRD.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The cut into the engine split. I agree, and it is a new fact against my recommendation of this morning, brd first: the elicitation per artefact is the first concrete case on which the mechanism/instance line can be drawn.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "One thing that does not fit before we carry it on: where do the definitions live after the cut? Is it meant as one dispatcher and two roots of definitions, the engine's + the local one?", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "i dont know how to split it. one idea is to have a real engine. a separate git and a light shell that handles things like ingest ledger.... or we make forge of thought the big engine, into which i install from separate gits (official and unofficial) something like plugins (brief, brd, test analyst, ...)", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Before I offer an opinion I will look at what already stands in the intent and in the research, so that I do not reopen what was rejected.", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 7.57}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: read THR.0230, THR.0190, REJ.0140–0150 and the research", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The two ideas are not alternatives, they are one thing seen from two ends: a thin shell means nothing without a place for \"the rest\", and plugins mean nothing without a shell to install into.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "My opinion, three points:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. The engine = what is the same for every framework and what a plugin cannot carry: CLAUDE.md as always-on context. The engine is the repository with CLAUDE.md and the mechanisms, a framework is a package of instances.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The cost is the one CHL.0110 named: the rules of particular artefacts must leave CLAUDE.md for the definitions, or there is nothing to package.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The installation mechanism is not to be decided now. That is a question for research.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Today's talk is, as I see it, already the opening of the brief engine-split. Nothing written; the birth of a brief is a step on your word – /forge brief engine-split.", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 12.5075}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "shouldnt we solve the elicitations first??", "typing": 2.1, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Yes, and I take back the order of my last answer. Three points, mine:", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. The elicitation can be solved in today's engine without a decision on the split. None of it waits on where the definitions will live.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The split gets cheaper by it, down to a move of files. Once the definitions are self-contained, engine-split is a decision about roots and installation, not about content.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The bound of the round: mechanism and shape only, no new artefact.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Carried in the conversation, nowhere: a new THR and the order elicitation → brd → engine-split. Do you want to open the round now as a walkthrough, or first write that THR into the intent?", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 11.2}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "shouldnt we make a brief on the elicitation?", "typing": 2.2, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Yes – it is exactly the case of Document chain 1: a whole of thinking that would otherwise fall into the intent as a batch of unverified positions. A brief has a lock and is the provenance anchor for what later moves from CLAUDE.md into the definitions.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "The step, on your word (/forge brief elicitation):", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- create projects/forge/00-brief-elicitation.md from templates/brief.md (the YAML header only, 0.1 draft) and 00-brief-elicitation.history.md from templates/history.md", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- add a row to the ledger, table Briefs, Mined: pending", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Nothing else: the content of today's conversation would go in as the first write on confirmation, once the brief exists.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The name elicitation – or do you want another?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 7.98}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "yes, elicitation", "typing": 0.8, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Creating the brief elicitation as the state file says: the header from the template, the history companion, the row in the ledger.", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 1.6225}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: read the templates of the brief and the history", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: created the brief, its history companion and the ledger", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "row", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Written:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/00-brief-elicitation.md – header 0.1 draft, body empty", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/00-brief-elicitation.history.md – row 0.1", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/ledger.md, table Briefs – row 0.1 / draft / pending", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "State: draft. Everything from today's conversation is so far only in the conversation, that is nowhere.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The brief is born here, so you moderate. One question to clarify: what exactly does the brief examine – only the elicitation of the chain artefacts, or elicitation as a mechanism of the forge in general, that is recipes too, the /setup interview, and possibly the way a reviewer hands its list into a walkthrough?", "n": 5, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 6.665}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 2, "time": "09:55", "title": "The disagreement", "caption": [["Now", "Claude asked what the brief examines and, among the options, named the handing of a reviewer's list into a walkthrough. The principal does not understand, then disagrees and offers his own definition: elicitation is a process of finding. Claude accepts, draws the consequences in three points and overshoots in one. The principal asks what is wrong with it, and Claude withdraws the point."], ["Why", "Disagreement is the normal course of the work: Claude says his opinion and carries it as his own, the principal holds the substance. What Claude overshoots he withdraws on one question, not after a defence."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "what is this? handing the reviewer's list into a walkthrough", "typing": 3.0, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I meant what happens after /critique, /challenge or /check: the reviewer produces a list (FND, CHL, the findings of a check) and that list is then walked with you item by item as a walkthrough.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "I named it as the edge case of the scope: is it elicitation or not? My opinion: it is not. The walkthrough of findings has its shape already and nothing per artefact is in it. Elicitation is what asks before an artefact exists or grows.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "So the question stays narrower: the chain artefacts only, or recipes and /setup too?", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 11.28}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "thats not elicitation. i dont take elicitation as any conversation of ours. elicitation in its meaning isnt even a conversation. its a process of finding. it fits the making of an artefact best. together we find the artefact. we form knowledge. agree ??", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 7.05}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I agree. Three points, mine:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Elicitation = a process of finding whose output is an artefact. The conversation is only the medium; the interview is one instrument, research and sources are others. With that my narrowing of today to \"how we ask\" falls too – a checklist is not a questionnaire but a map of what must be found for the artefact to be complete. How it is found is the situation's.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The consequence for the scope: a recipe and /setup do not fall under this definition whole. Composing a recipe is configuration from known options, not the finding of knowledge.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The consequence for the forge's vocabulary: CLAUDE.md today has the working method Elicitation interview. By your definition it is misnamed – the interview is the shape, elicitation is the process.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Your definition is the first piece for the brief, carried, nowhere yet.", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 13.885}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "whats wrong with it? Elicitation interview for me elicitation is what we do and the interview is the form. or am i off?", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 2.05}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "You are not off, I overshot. \"Elicitation interview\" = the interview as a form of elicitation, exactly as you say; the name is fine.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "What I wanted to say and said wrongly: today the interview is the only form of elicitation the forge names, and the paragraph in CLAUDE.md describes only that form. The process itself – what is found for which artefact, and that it is found by research and sources too, not by questions alone – has no place of its own anywhere. I withdraw point 3; what stays: the brief has to name the process, the form is done.", "n": 7, "pre": false}, {"t": "Carried: your definition, plus this correction as mine. Nowhere yet.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 10.6725}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 3, "time": "10:01", "title": "The preview of a write", "caption": [["Now", "The principal wants to see what the write would look like. Claude shows the body of the brief 0.2 as it would stand in the file: in English, since the brief is in the project's language, the principal's pieces translated and unmarked, Claude's blocks marked. Then he asks whether to write. The principal says: talk on first, then write it all at once."], ["Why", "A preview is a tool: concrete text sharpens the reaction. The write happens once at the end of the round, on the principal's word; until then everything is \"nowhere yet\"."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "preview of the write", "typing": 1.0, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Preview of the write – 00-brief-elicitation.md 0.2, the body under the header. Your pieces translated, unmarked; my blocks (Claude). Nothing written yet.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Where the elicitation lives today", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Where does the elicitation of an artefact live today — the way we talk over a brief, an intent and so on? Is it in CLAUDE.md, or in the agents and skills?", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "(Claude) Three layers, each with a different role. CLAUDE.md carries principles only: prime directive 1, the working methods and Document chain 1–3. The walkthrough skill carries the shape of the conversation shared by everything. The /forge state files carry what differs per artefact: brief.md, intent.md, assignment.md. The agents take no part: critic, challenger and check are isolated reviewers that never see the conversation.", "n": 7, "pre": false}, {"t": "Per artefact", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Where do we define how the elicitation runs? It should be different for every artefact: we talk one way over a brief, another over an intent, and a wholly different way over a BRD. Every artefact has its template.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "(Claude) The mechanism for that already exists: /forge <state> resolves the state file (how we ask) and the artefact's template (what is to come out); a new artefact is a new pair of files and the dispatcher never changes. The pair is unbalanced today: nowhere is there a list of what a given artefact needs to have found before it is complete. The precedent exists inside the forge: /recipe <genre> carries an explicit numbered elicitation checklist and points at its skeleton. That is the pair the chain artefacts lack.", "n": 8, "pre": false}, {"t": "Framed, and user-definable — where to stop", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "I want the elicitation framed. And it should be user-definable: just as I want a user-defined check, I may want a user-defined elicitation. But that leads on to user-defined templates and user-defined artefacts, and I am not sure where to stop.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "(Claude) The boundary already exists and only needs naming: mechanism versus instance. The engine never defines an instance, the user never changes the mechanism. The test is simple: does CLAUDE.md have to change for it? If not, it is THR.0300; if yes, it is a derivation (THR.0420).", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: one mechanism, one shape …", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The split: two ideas …", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Order …", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "What elicitation is", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Elicitation is not any conversation of ours. Elicitation, in its meaning, is not even a conversation. It is a process of finding. It fits the making of an artefact best: together we find the artefact; we form knowledge.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "(Claude) Agreed, with three consequences. The conversation is only the medium; the interview is one instrument, research and sources are others. So a checklist is not a questionnaire but a map of what must be found for the artefact to be complete; how it is found is the situation's. Scope: composing a recipe is largely configuration from known options, not the finding of knowledge, and /setup is not at all. The walkthrough of a reviewer's findings is not elicitation either: it has its shape already and nothing per artefact in it.", "n": 8, "pre": false}, {"t": "Elicitation interview: elicitation is what we do, the interview is the form.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(Claude) Correct; an earlier remark of mine that the name was wrong is withdrawn. The brief names the process; the form is done.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "History 0.2: \"First body: the whole of the conversation of 2026-09-28 …\" – last_change the same; ledger Briefs row to 0.2.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Do you want it written like this (write), or something changed?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "lets talk on first and then write it all at once", "typing": 2.4000000000000004, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Fine, I carry the preview, we write at once.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 4, "time": "10:40", "title": "The proposed definition", "caption": [["Now", "The principal asks for an example: what the definition of the elicitation would look like for the brief. Claude compiles the morning into a proposal in seven blocks, in English, as if it were the file, and says himself where he is least sure. The principal asks: is it not too long, does it not clash with CLAUDE.md, where did the inspiration go? Claude answers three times honestly and rewrites the block Partner."], ["Why", "A concrete proposal is a tool, not a result: it gives the principal something to react to. Claude proposes and says where he doubts; what does not hold he rewrites, and still nothing is written."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "make me an example of how it would be defined for the brief. compile what we said, make your proposal so i can see it", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "A proposal of states/brief.md in seven blocks – a compilation of today, in English, as if it were the file. A draft, written nowhere.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "description: Compose or finish a brief — the principal's own text of one whole of thinking, gathered as widely as it can be, locked when done", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Target 00-brief.md (bare) or 00-brief-<name>.md. Shape of the result: templates/brief.md — a YAML header, then free form, no IDs, no conventions of the chain. What a brief is: CLAUDE.md, Document chain 1.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "Inputs The principal's thought, however it arrives. Around it, gathered during the elicitation: research notes, sources and Claude's own proposals. The existing intent and ledger are read only to know what already stands, never to shape the text.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "Aim The brief gathers the thought as widely as it can be gathered: the principal's idea and every idea, inspiration and counter-example around it, from his head and from the world outside, kept as one whole that holds together. Nothing is yet sorted by weight, nothing is a position: the brief is the pile, the intent is where it is sorted. The brief is complete when the principal says he has nothing more to put in and locks it.", "n": 8, "pre": false}, {"t": "Partner Claude steers the finding, the principal steers the decisions. Claude inspires and confronts: he brings how the same thing is done elsewhere, says how original an idea is and where it repeats the known, verifies what can be verified before he answers, raises a wrong assumption at once (CLAUDE.md, prime directive 1), and puts concrete proposals in front of the principal so that the reaction is sharp (Working methods, Draft early). He draws the thought out where it is terse — to get it out in a form that can be understood and tested, not to add his own. He does not sort, does not decide what stays, does not introduce IDs, and does not tidy the principal's words. What he contributes is marked: a finding (how X works, a verified fact, literature) becomes a research note and is cited; a proposal (a design, a comparison, a \"take / leave\" of what exists) enters the brief as a block opening with (Claude); a source's contribution as (source: <path>). Each answer ends with the few questions Claude cannot decide, never a questionnaire.", "n": 17, "pre": false}, {"t": "Map The brief has no required content. What the elicitation nevertheless finds, whatever the form:", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the thought in the principal's words — what he wants and why;", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the world around it — what exists that does the same or the opposite, and what of it is inspiration, counter-example or proof that the wheel exists;", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the material — the sources and research the thought rests on, gathered and registered, so that the intent can cite them.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Instruments", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- /research <topic> — durable findings into research/, indexed; a step of the elicitation, proposed by Claude and run on the principal's word.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- /ingest [file] — outside material into sources/, registered and indexed, on the principal's word.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Draft early, Reflect back, In pieces, Elicitation interview — CLAUDE.md, Working methods.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Course", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Resolve the project and the file; create the brief from the template if it does not exist; a locked brief is not edited.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. However the text arrives – pasted whole, begun outside, or born here – Claude works from the first word as the Partner says and accumulates the principal's answers as his text, not as a summary.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. Write once per round on his confirmation.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. Lock only on his explicit word: version 1.0, status approved.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "5. End by naming the state and, if locked, proposing /forge intent.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Where I am least sure: Map – three things that are found even though the brief has no required content. The alternative is to leave Map out entirely and let Aim stand in for it.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "questions isnt it too long? wont it clash with the already long claude.md? the inspiration and creativity that belong to your role have gone out of it", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Three honest answers:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Yes, long. 90 lines against today's 69, and half of it is restatement: Target and Inputs repeat CLAUDE.md, Course copies today's steps. A definition has to cite, not repeat. Estimate after the cut: about 40 lines.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. It does not clash with CLAUDE.md by length but by repetition. The state file is loaded only on /forge brief and adds nothing to the always-on context.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The creativity has gone, you are right. My Partner degenerated into a verifier. Inspiration is not only \"how they do it elsewhere\" – it is also ideas of his own unasked, alternatives, analogies from other fields, the provocation \"what if\". The order should be inspire first, then confront, not the other way round.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "The rewritten Partner, the only block that changes in substance:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Partner. Claude steers the finding, the principal steers the decisions. Claude inspires first: brings ideas of his own unasked, alternatives, analogies from other fields, a \"what if\" that turns the thought around — all marked as his. Then he confronts: how the same thing is done elsewhere, how original an idea is and where the wheel already exists, what can be verified before answering, a wrong assumption raised at once. He draws the thought out where it is terse and puts concrete proposals in front of the principal so the reaction is sharp. He does not sort, does not decide what stays, does not introduce IDs, does not tidy the principal's words. A finding becomes a research note, cited; a proposal enters as (Claude); a source as (source: <path>). Each answer ends with the few questions Claude cannot decide.", "n": 13, "pre": false}, {"t": "The other blocks I cut down to citations; Map I leave to be decided.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 5, "time": "10:45", "title": "The walkthrough", "caption": [["Now", "The principal reads the first sentence of Partner and sees in it what has gone: the partnership. Claude proposes another first sentence, the principal answers with one letter. Claude moves to the next item, the Map, says what would change, recommends and asks. One letter again."], ["Why", "The walkthrough: one item per message, for each what would change and a recommendation, the verdict in one word. The verdicts are carried in the conversation and written once, at the end of the round."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "Claude steers the finding, the principal steers the decisions. were still running in the mode that i decide, but whether in the first sentence we havent lost that partnership", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "You are right – that sentence divides the work into two helms, and \"together we find\" means one. The deciding stays yours, but that is a sentence about the end, not about the beginning.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "A proposal of the first sentence:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Claude and the principal find the thought together, neither waiting for the other: Claude brings as much as the principal does, and what stays is the principal's to say.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "The rest of the block unchanged – \"inspires first … then confronts … draws out … does not sort, does not decide what stays\" already carries the partnership; only the opening sentence denied it.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 14.774999999999999}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted: the block Partner with the new opening sentence, carried into the brief.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The next item, the last open one of the brief – Map. The situation: the brief is the only artefact with no required content, so a map of \"what must be found\" threatens to become required content through the back door. Yet without it the lock has no support but \"the principal said enough\", and /forge intent does not know what to look for when mining.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "What would change: with the three items of the map Claude has something to offer during the elicitation when the conversation stalls, and at the lock he can say \"we have not been through the world around it\" – as a recommendation, not a gate (prime directive 5).", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "Recommendation: keep the map, with the first sentence \"The brief has no required content\" as the safeguard, so that it stays a map of the finding, not a template.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted: Map stays, with the safeguard \"no required content\". The definition of the brief is thereby done as the example – seven blocks, Partner and Map as of today, the rest shortened to citations.", "n": 4, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 3.37}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 6, "time": "11:15", "title": "The write", "caption": [["Now", "After an hour of walkthrough the principal says the word write. Claude does not write at once: first he shows the outline of the whole as it would stand in the file, and asks. The principal still asks whether the accepted wordings will be lost. Then he says yes and Claude writes: the file, the version, the line count, what did not change and what is not saved."], ["Why", "One write per round, on the principal's word, and before it a reflection, so that the write confirms rather than surprises. What is written has a file name and a section; what is not is said aloud."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "write", "typing": 0.25, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Before the write a reflection of the whole – brief 0.2, in English, your words unmarked, my remarks only as (Claude: …) where a reservation remained. The outline:", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Where the elicitation lives today – three layers, the agents outside, the precedent of the genre files.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. What elicitation is – a process of finding, not a conversation; the interview is the form; the map before the template, the template the shape of the result.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The shape of a definition – seven blocks; Aim = state, Partner = conduct, nothing twice.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. Brief – Aim, Partner (partnership, inspiration first), Map with three things (Claude: the uncertain point), research and ingest as steps.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "5. Intent – Aim with the sorting, the horizon and the final reality check; Partner conduct only.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "6. Assignment – questions only on the difference, the recast with the provenance map, the walkthrough by group.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "7. Horizon – mandatory in the BRD, free in the intent, optional in the assignment.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "8. Marks in a brief – no authorship; only (source: <path>) and (Claude: …) for a reservation not adopted.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "9. One mechanism, user-definable – mechanism versus instance, the test \"does CLAUDE.md have to change?\".", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "10. The split and the order – the order elicitation → brd → engine-split.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The write: 00-brief-elicitation.md → 0.2 (body + last_change), history row 0.2, ledger Briefs row 0.2 + Note. Nothing in the intent, nothing in CLAUDE.md.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Yes?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "will you write the wordings of the individual states in there too? or do we lose them and do them again in the intent?", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The wordings I write whole, verbatim, as they were accepted – the brief is the pile and the state file says \"store as shown, never re-narrated\": for the brief Aim, Partner, Map and the shortened rest; for the intent and the assignment Aim and Partner.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "None of it is lost; at mining they become positions and the positions become state files. Lost is only what stayed in the conversation and is not in the brief – that is why I write everything.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "The write as reflected. Yes?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 9.665000000000001}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "yes", "typing": 0.15000000000000002, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Writing brief 0.2, the history and the ledger.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 0.6}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: 00-brief-elicitation.md, body 0.2", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: history row 0.2, ledger row, wrap check", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Written:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/00-brief-elicitation.md → 0.2, draft, 497 lines, ten sections.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 00-brief-elicitation.history.md – row 0.2, last_change agrees.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- ledger.md, Briefs – 0.2 / draft / pending, Note updated.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Nothing in the intent, nothing in CLAUDE.md, nothing in the state files – that comes at mining. Nothing saved to git (/save on your word).", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "State of the brief: draft. The next step, a recommendation: either elicit further, or lock 1.0 and /forge intent to mine it – after today I would not lock yet.", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 4.9825}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 7, "time": "14:34", "title": "The critique from outside", "caption": [["Now", "In the afternoon the principal brings a file: a critique of the brief by another tool. Claude registers it as a source and asks what it is for; the role of a source is the principal's to say. Then Claude reads the brief and the critique, writes the difference in five sections, proposes an order of eleven points by weight and opens the walkthrough with point 1: not to narrow the brief, only to say what it is about."], ["Why", "A source from outside is first stored and registered, nothing more; what is taken from it the principal decides. A critique informs, it does not decide: Claude says where it is right and where it misses the forge, and every point is the principal's verdict."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "/ingest forge-elicitation-brief-review.md forge", "typing": 2.35, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Glob: found the file in projects/forge/sources/", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: sources/00-INDEX.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: sources/forge-elicitation-brief-review.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: sources/00-INDEX.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: ledger.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Registered: projects/forge/sources/forge-elicitation-brief-review.md (text, date 2026-09-28, origin of the date ingested). The file already lay in sources/, I copied and changed nothing. The record is in sources/00-INDEX.md (a new entry, Role and Use for still —) and in ledger.md, table Sources.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "Nothing new for the intent directly: the source concerns the brief elicitation 0.2 in progress, against which it carries seventeen reservations with proposed wording and candidate definitions of the brief, the intent and the assignment.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "What is it to serve?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 7.7775}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "its a critique from copilot about our elicitation brief. we make the difference, analyse it, take the good, get inspired, fix.", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 1.55}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: 00-brief-elicitation.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: the skill walkthrough", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: the state file brief.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: sources/00-INDEX.md, the field Use for", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The difference: the critique against the brief elicitation 0.2", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "The result in one sentence: the critique agrees with the brief at the core, brings about ten useful corrections and filling for the missing blocks, and in three things misses how the forge works.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Where they agree Elicitation as finding, not a conversation. Map, process and template as three things. Seven blocks. Partner in place of Role. Three phases of the assignment with a provenance map. The order: elicitation first, then the split.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. Justified reservations about the wording of the brief", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 2.3, 2.4: \"He does not sort\" and at the same time \"one whole that holds together\" – distinguish arranging from deciding.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 2.5: \"as widely as it can be gathered\" – the outside world cannot be exhausted; the lock means \"enough for the next step\".", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 2.2: \"Claude brings as much as the principal\" – a measure of quantity, not of initiative.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 2.10: completion is described by both Aim and Course – one condition in two places.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 2.8: epistemic status is in the inspiration, missing in the definition – a real gap.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. What the critique adds A map of the brief in six areas, checked only at the end. The marks (proposal), (verified), (unverified), (hypothesis) – a new convention, so your decision. The missing blocks Map, Instruments and Course for the intent and the assignment. The fate of every part of the brief at mining. Rules for empty blocks, stopping a research, negative findings, ten behavioural scenarios.", "n": 7, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. Where the critique misses the forge It reads the brief as a decision document – in the forge a brief decides nothing, the intent sorts. The candidate definitions repeat shared rules – the brief wants the opposite: \"cites, never restates\". The line count as a criterion of success – the brief gives it only as an estimate of the effect.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "5. My own finding, outside the critique The brief says in the block Partner \"Each answer ends with the few questions\", but in Instruments it cites the Elicitation interview, which has one question per message. It is a contradiction inside the brief.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "The proposed order of the walkthrough, by weight", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. The scope of the brief (2.1)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. Marks and epistemic status (2.7, 2.8)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The map of the brief (2.6)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. Arrange, or decide (2.3, 2.4)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "5. Several questions, or one (2.13 and my finding)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "6. The completion of the brief (2.5) and the ownership of the blocks (2.10 to 2.12)", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "7. The wording on Claude's contribution (2.2)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "8. Research: starting, stopping, negative findings (2.9, 2.14, 2.15)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "9. The missing blocks of the intent and the assignment, the fate of the parts of the brief", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "10. Scenarios and migration (2.16, 2.17)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "11. The horizon in the BRD and the number of questions (section 8, 3.10)", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Everything agreed I carry in the conversation, and it goes into the brief in one write at the end of the round, as version 0.3. Until then none of it is written anywhere.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Shall we start the walkthrough with point 1, the scope of the brief?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted: the walkthrough runs, in the proposed order. I carry the verdicts in the conversation, they are written nowhere yet.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Point 1 of 11: the scope of the brief (critique 2.1)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "What the critique says. The brief allegedly mixes three decisions of different maturity: the shape of a definition, the elicitation of three artefacts and the architecture (the split of the engine, plugins, local roots, the BRD, the merging of /recipe with /forge). Whoever accepts the elicitation looks as if he accepted the undecided architecture too. It proposes to narrow the brief and move the architecture into work of its own.", "n": 7, "pre": false}, {"t": "What stands in the brief. The architecture is in two sections at the end: \"One mechanism, user-definable, and where to stop\" and \"The split, and the order of the work\". The brief itself says the installation is \"a research question, not a decision for now\", and gives the order elicitation, brd, engine-split.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "My view. The critique is right about the risk, not about the cure. In the forge a brief decides nothing, it is the pile and the intent sorts. Striking the two sections would go against the rule \"more in the brief, cleaning in the intent\". But the risk at mining is real, and one sentence removes it.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "What would change. Brief 0.3 gets one paragraph, nothing is deleted. At mining the matter of the split goes into threads (THR.0230, THR.0190, THR.0300), not into positions.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "The proposal. Against the critique's recommendation, not to narrow the brief. At the start of the section \"One mechanism, user-definable, and where to stop\" insert:", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "What this brief is about is the elicitation: the shape of a definition and the definitions of the brief, the intent and the assignment. Everything from here on (the extension point for a user's own definitions, the split of the engine, the installation, the unifying of /recipe with /forge) is carried as a consequence and as material for the briefs brd and engine-split; nothing of it is decided here. Self-contained definitions are the prerequisite of a later split, never the other way round.", "n": 8, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted: point 1, the brief is not narrowed and the paragraph on the scope goes to the start of the section, as shown. Only in the conversation so far.", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 8, "time": "16:06", "title": "The principal holds the shape", "caption": [["Now", "After another round of walkthrough over wording the principal says what a brief should be: at most one A4 of free text. Claude admits the mistake, they were making an intent and calling it a brief, and shows it in numbers. He does not write the version 0.4 he offered and says where everything now is. The principal decides: finish the brief, throw nothing away, put the lesson into the definition of the brief's elicitation."], ["Why", "The principal holds the shape of the artefact; Claude is responsible for the discipline of the process and, where it failed, says so without a defence. What is not written is not lost: it is said where it lies."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "feedback. the brief on the elicitation in my mind is max one a4 of free text where i write that i want personas what elicitation is i write paragraphs there like \"a brief is a free structure for putting an idea together. that is then chiselled. a brief isnt perfect and shouldnt be overly detailed either. it happened to me that i chiselled the brief so far that no work was actually left for the intent. thats not good. but then again its not a map of everything we went through. on the ground of research ingestion my ideas your ideas make decisions about what goes into the brief and what doesnt.\" and on that we make the intent, where we write the maps decide on the 7 blocks describe the elicitor. again we are making an intent instead of a brief TBH", "typing": 3.5000000000000004, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: a note into Claude's memory", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: the index of the memory", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "You are right. We were making an intent and calling it a brief. The mistake is mine: structure and the discipline of the process are my work, and I led you through two rounds of walkthrough over wording that does not belong in a brief.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "What happened, in numbers", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Scope: your idea at most one A4; the reality about 580 lines. Content: what I want and why, in free text; the reality three definitions in seven blocks, maps, exact wordings. Today's work: write down the idea; the reality 26 verdicts over wording.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "Exactly what you yourself warned against: a brief chiselled so far that no work is left for the intent.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "What it means for the write in preparation", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Version 0.4 as I offered it I do not write. It would add further maps and blocks to the brief, that is even more intent.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Where everything now is", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "brief 0.2 – saved in git brief 0.3, the long one – on disk only, not saved the 11 verdicts of today – in the conversation only, nowhere else", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Today's work is not lost, only in the wrong place. It is material for the intent.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The next step", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "The short brief should be in your words. The paragraph you just quoted is its core. Will you write it yourself, or shall I put it together from your sentences of today, verbatim and unedited, and show it to you?", "n": 4, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "for me lets just finish that brief with what you have so it isnt thrown away. rather we have to learn from that feedback so we define the brief's elicitor right. no need to simplify that brief by force now. we already did it so lets finish it. but then lets make a better elicitation of the brief according to that feedback. write this decision into the brief so we see it and lets go on. and analyse how this feedback would affect how we have the brief's elicitation defined.", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Understood: we finish this brief as it is, nothing is thrown away and nothing is shortened by force. The lesson we use for a better definition of the brief's elicitation. Nothing is written in the project yet, the write waits for your yes.", "n": 4, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 9, "time": "17:58", "title": "Research before the lock", "caption": [["Now", "In the evening the principal asks whether the brief is ready for the lock. Claude reads the brief, its history and both reviews and answers: yes, with one empty area of the map and two small things that cannot be mended after the lock. The principal proposes two researches and wants Claude's opinion; Claude splits them, recommends locking first, and the principal decides the other way. The researches run, the two small things are accepted, and when the researches return Claude says what they confirm, what they put in question and what he proposes."], ["Why", "A research is a step of the elicitation: Claude proposes it against a named need, it runs only on the principal's word, and after it Claude says what it changed and what not. A recommendation is said once; a declined one is not re-argued."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "look at the brief elicitation, is it ready to lock in your view?", "typing": 3.2, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: 00-brief-elicitation.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: 00-brief-elicitation.history.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: the state file brief.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: sources/forge-elicitation-brief-review-v0.4.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Grep: research/00-INDEX.md for \"elicit\"", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "My opinion: yes, the brief is ready to be locked. I wrote nothing, I only read the brief, its history and both reviews.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Three points, all mine:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Another round would harm it. The brief has three rounds in one day and two reviews behind it; the remaining reservations you knowingly left to the intent. All seven places marked \"to be decided at mining\" are in order, not a debt.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. One area of its own map is empty: the world around it. No research on how elicitation is done elsewhere is in research/. It does not stand in the way of the lock, the area may stay empty, only it should be a conscious decision.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. Two small things that cannot be mended after the lock. The opening note says \"some 580 lines\" and \"two rounds of walkthrough\"; the brief has 717 lines today and the rounds were three. And the brief refers to a file in tmp/, which is gitignored, so the locked brief will forever cite a file that is not in the repository.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "Do you want to lock the brief as it is, or first mend the two small things of point 3?", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "imo doing a research is a good thing and we should do two: one on our definitions of the brief, the intent and the assignment and a second on how to define elicitation between a human and an ai over artefacts in general. ??", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "My opinion: two researches are right and the split into two fits. I write nothing, these are only my three points.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. They really are two different questions. The first asks about the result: what the brief, the intent and the assignment should contain and when each is done. The second asks about the way: how a human and an AI get to an artefact together.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The first question I would put to the outside, not to our text. \"A research on our definitions\" invites a third review of the brief. A more useful brief is: how the layers between an idea and a handover are defined elsewhere and what \"done\" means in each. None of it verified, that is exactly the research's work.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. I recommend locking first, the research as the first step of the mining. This brief has shown already that every new impulse starts another round in it. Against it stands one thing: the area \"the world around it\" stays empty in the brief, and knowingly.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "Both researches reach the web, so I start them only on your explicit word, each on its own through /research.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Do you want to lock first and research at mining, or research before the lock?", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "do the research before the lock. well see what the researches return and either we finish the brief or we lock.", "typing": 3.4999999999999996, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Skill: research artefact-layers-between-idea-and-handover forge", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Agent: research of the artefact layers from idea to handover", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Agent: research of elicitation between a human and an AI", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Grep: the reference to the file in tmp/ across the forge", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Understood. I have written nothing yet, the change is only here in the conversation. Both researches are still running.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The proposed change: the reference is in the repository in one place only, the section \"Inspiration: a preparation done outside the forge\". New:", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "The conversation was taken from the preparation of another project and is not kept here.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The write: I carry the change and write it in one write together with what comes out of the researches. It will be one version 0.6, not a version of its own for one sentence.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 9.975000000000001}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted. I carry the new wording in the conversation, it is not in the file yet.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The second small thing before the lock: the opening note of the brief gives two numbers that no longer hold. The proposal: drop the numbers, the sense of the sentence stays.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "It grew far too long, with three definitions worded block by block and several rounds over exact wording", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The reason: after the lock the sentence can no longer be mended, and a number without a date goes stale with every write.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 9.045}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted. I carry both changes in the conversation, nothing is in the file yet. Both researches are still running. As soon as they return I check the drafts, write the notes into research/ with the index and the ledger, and sum up for you what follows from them for the brief.", "n": 5, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 4.4}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: the draft of research 1 from the agent", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "WebFetch: verified the quotations at four sources", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: research/2026-09-28-artefact-layers-from-idea-to-handover.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: the draft of research 2 from the agent", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Both researches have returned. The first note is written in research/, for the second I am now verifying the key numbers at the source before I write it.", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 2.84}, {"k": "tool", "text": "WebFetch: verified four studies at the source", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: research/2026-09-28-human-ai-elicitation-over-artefacts.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: research/00-INDEX.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: ledger.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Both researches are done and written. The brief has held, as I see it: nothing found refutes it, two things put it in question and belong to the intent.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "What is written: both notes whole in research/, two new entries in research/00-INDEX.md, two new rows in ledger.md, table Research. The two changes to the brief (the reference to another project, the numbers in the opening note) are still only in the conversation.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "What the researches say", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "They confirm:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Three layers are a common shape, but nobody has our three. It is the forge's own cut.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Elicitation as a process with several instruments, of which the conversation is only one, is the consensus of the disciplines.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Done is nowhere proven, it is always confirmed by the owner. Our \"the principal locks\" matches it.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- A map that is not a questionnaire exists in practice (spec-kit: one question at a time, at most five, at the end the state of every area).", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The block Partner has no counterpart outside. No tool says whose the words are.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "They put in question:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Four controlled studies agree: the further an AI goes into the writing, the better the text and the weaker the sense of ownership. Without AI 6.74 of 7, with a draft from AI 4.28. Goals written by a model people met in 46.6 % of cases, their own in 72.8 %.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "- That touches two places of the brief: the active Claude at the opening and \"draft early to the extreme\". The limit: the studies are short tasks with laypeople, not an expert over his own document.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Mind the word: elsewhere \"brief\" means a short assignment for someone else, not one's own raw idea.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Reliability: the key quotations and numbers I verified by a second independent reading and they agree. The standards and doctrines could not be opened at the source, they are cited second-hand only and the notes say so.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "My proposal: do not rewrite the brief. Write version 0.6 with three changes and then lock:", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. the reference to another project without its name (accepted),", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. the numbers in the opening note gone (accepted),", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. new, one sentence that these two researches belong to the brief, so that the intent can cite them.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Everything else from the researches, both questionings included, is decided at the mining into the intent. The reason: they are questions to decide, and the brief itself says a tension may stay in it.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 10, "time": "18:36", "title": "The lock", "caption": [["Now", "The principal says write and Claude writes version 0.6: file by file, what changed. Then he shows what the lock would do and asks. The principal says: yes, lock it. Claude locks and confirms: version 1.0, status approved, the text unchanged, immutable from this moment."], ["Why", "The write and the lock are two steps, each on the principal's own word, each with a preview before it. The lock does not change the text; it changes what may be done with it: from now on the brief is only mined."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "write", "typing": 0.25, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: 00-brief-elicitation.md (four times)", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: 00-brief-elicitation.history.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: ledger.md (three times)", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Written. The brief is at version 0.6, status draft, not locked.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "What is where: the header – version 0.6, a new last_change; the opening note – the numbers dropped; the section \"Inspiration\" – the reference replaced by a sentence without the project's name; a new section \"The world around it\" – cites both researches; the history – row 0.6, three changes with reasons; the ledger – version 0.6.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "Nothing unwritten remains in the conversation. Nothing went to git, saving is a step of its own (/save).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The next step: the lock", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "On your word I will do this:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 00-brief-elicitation.md: version 1.0, status approved, immutable from then on", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 00-brief-elicitation.history.md: row 1.0 on the lock", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- ledger.md: the brief's row to 1.0 approved, Mined stays pending, the row under Waiting changes from \"waits for the lock\" to \"waits for the mining\"", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "The reason: the brief is done in your view and in mine, the researches did not refute it and the rest belongs to the intent.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Shall I lock the brief?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 11.217500000000001}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "yes lock it", "typing": 0.55, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: 00-brief-public-engine.md and its history (the model of a", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "lock)", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 0.6}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: 00-brief-elicitation.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: 00-brief-elicitation.history.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: ledger.md (three times)", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The brief is locked: 00-brief-elicitation.md, version 1.0, status approved. From this moment it does not change.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "What is written: the header – version 1.0, approved, last_change on the lock; the history – row 1.0: locked; the ledger – 1.0 approved, Mined pending, the brief waits for the mining.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "The text of the brief did not change at the lock. Nothing unwritten remains in the conversation. Nothing has gone to git yet.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Recommendation: first /save, then /forge intent and the mining of the brief. The reason: the locked brief and the two researches are a closed whole, and the mining will be a long round, better begun from a clean state.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "Do you want to save now, or go straight to the mining?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 9.73}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 11, "time": "18:46", "title": "The mining", "caption": [["Now", "The principal answers with one word: mining. Claude opens the state intent, reads the locked brief, the whole intent, both research notes and the definition of the state, and proposes the order in which to mine the brief, one whole per message. He writes nothing; he carries everything until the word write."], ["Why", "A locked brief is mined into the intent whole by whole, and the intent is where the sorting happens: positions, threads, rejections. The video ends here; the mining is other work and another video."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "mining", "typing": 0.30000000000000004, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Skill: forge intent forge", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: the state file intent.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: the skill walkthrough", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: 10-intent.md (4.31)", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I have read the locked brief, the whole intent (4.31), both research notes and the definition of the state intent. The mining can begin. I write nothing, I carry everything in the conversation until the word write.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "The proposed course of the mining: the brief has eleven wholes. I propose to take them in this order, one whole per message:", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. What elicitation is (a process of finding, not a conversation; map, process, template) – a new position", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The shape of a definition (seven blocks, the shared mechanism outside) – a new position", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. What a brief holds: the principal's choice, not the pile – turns POS.0110 and REJ.0180", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. The Partner of the brief: who writes, what Claude may do", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "5. The marks in a brief and the certainty of a claim", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "6. The rest of the brief's definition (Aim, Map, Instruments, Course)", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "7. The definition of the intent, with the place for the recipients, the objective and the criteria", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "8. The definition of the assignment (three phases, the provenance map)", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "9. The horizon in three layers", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "10. Mechanism against instance, user definitions", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "11. The split of the engine and the order of the work", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "I order by dependency, not by weight. The hardest is whole 3, because it turns a standing decision of 14 September. But it rests on what elicitation is and what a definition looks like, which is why wholes 1 and 2 come before it.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "What the mining does: positions, threads and rejections in 10-intent.md, one write at the end as version 4.32. No change in CLAUDE.md, in the state files or in the templates.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Do you agree with this course and order?", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "card", "title": "What to take away", "text": ["A brief is found by questions: Claude asks, proposes and says his opinion; the principal answers and decides.", "Nothing is written without the principal's word; what is only in the conversation is nowhere yet.", "A reviewer and a research are steps the principal orders and judges.", "The lock is his explicit act."], "dur": 8.5}]});
